WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:14.063
It was a very warm evening in the jungle.

2
00:00:15.604 --> 00:00:19.065
The moon shone brightly into the mouth of the wolves' cave.

3
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.569
Father Wolf woke up from his day's rest and yawned.

4
00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:30.232
Mother Wolf lay nearby.

5
00:00:31.196 --> 00:00:34.699
She kept her nose on their four tumbling, squealing cubs.

6
00:00:36.921 --> 00:00:38.342
Father Wolf stretched.

7
00:00:38.362 --> 00:00:42.666
"It's time to hunt again, Mother."

8
00:00:43.727 --> 00:00:48.951
Just then a shadow with a bushy tail appeared at the entrance of the cave.

9
00:00:49.972 --> 00:00:51.193
Father Wolf frowned.

10
00:00:52.034 --> 00:00:54.076
It was Tabaqui, the jackal.

11
00:00:54.816 --> 00:00:59.020
The wolves disliked Tabaqui because he was always looking for food.

12
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:05.001
They were afraid of him too, because he was cunning and had a bad temper.

13
00:01:07.182 --> 00:01:12.063
Sometimes he ran madly through the forest, biting everything in his way.

14
00:01:14.284 --> 00:01:20.205
When Tabaqui acted like that, even the fierce tiger, Shere Khan, stayed away from him.

15
00:01:20.225 --> 00:01:25.127
"I'm hungry," Tabaqui announced.

16
00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:32.001
"Come inside and look around, Tabaqui," Father Wolf said with a sigh.

17
00:01:32.021 --> 00:01:34.302
"But I promise you.

18
00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:36.242
There is no food here."

19
00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:40.204
"I might find something," Tabaqui replied.

20
00:01:42.184 --> 00:01:45.626
He slunk toward the back of the cave and sniffed around.

21
00:01:48.487 --> 00:01:51.528
Soon he found an old bone with a scrap of meat.

22
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.241
"Thanks for the good meal," he said, licking his lips.

23
00:02:03.761 --> 00:02:05.782
He stared at the tiny wolf cubs.

24
00:02:05.802 --> 00:02:10.163
"I must say, your children are beautiful."

25
00:02:11.604 --> 00:02:14.004
Mother Wolf moved closer to her cubs.

26
00:02:15.145 --> 00:02:17.845
She and Father exchanged nervous glances.

27
00:02:17.865 --> 00:02:26.348
"Oh, by the way," Tabaqui went on, "Shere Khan has found some new hunting grounds.

28
00:02:27.136 --> 00:02:30.517
He told me he will be hunting here for a while."

29
00:02:30.537 --> 00:02:34.378
"Here?" Mother Wolf said in surprise.

30
00:02:34.398 --> 00:02:37.759
"But he has no right to hunt here!"

31
00:02:38.259 --> 00:02:39.519
Father Wolf exclaimed.

32
00:02:39.539 --> 00:02:42.540
"Shere Khan must stay near the river.

33
00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.761
That's the law of the jungle!"

34
00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:46.681
Tabaqui laughed.

35
00:02:48.062 --> 00:02:51.463
"Shall I tell him about your concern?"

36
00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:56.404
"Out!" Father Wolf snapped at the jackal.

37
00:02:57.228 --> 00:02:59.369
"Go hunt with your master, Tabaqui.

38
00:02:59.729 --> 00:03:01.669
You've bothered us enough for one night."

39
00:03:07.411 --> 00:03:10.112
will go," Tabaqui said quietly.

40
00:03:10.132 --> 00:03:14.793
"But remember my warning about Shere Khan's new hunting place.

41
00:03:15.593 --> 00:03:17.374
You can hear him right now, in fact.

42
00:03:18.454 --> 00:03:20.935
He's below, hunting among the bushes."

43
00:03:23.896 --> 00:03:27.533
After Tabaqui was gone, Father Wolf stepped out of the cave.

44
00:03:31.556 --> 00:03:36.620
Below in the valley, he could indeed hear the low snarls of a tiger.

45
00:03:38.821 --> 00:03:41.283
Mother Wolf came out and stood beside him.

46
00:03:41.303 --> 00:03:47.468
"It sounds like Shere Khan is not hunting animals tonight.

47
00:03:48.248 --> 00:03:50.390
I think he is hunting humans."

48
00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.452
Father Wolf flashed his white teeth.

49
00:03:54.584 --> 00:03:57.705
"There are plenty of beetles and frogs in the jungle.

50
00:03:58.505 --> 00:04:00.506
Why must that tiger hunt humans?"

51
00:04:01.726 --> 00:04:02.926
Mother Wolf grunted.

52
00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:08.128
An important law ruled the jungle.

53
00:04:09.328 --> 00:04:11.849
Animals were not supposed to hunt humans.

54
00:04:14.149 --> 00:04:18.271
The tiger's snarls grew louder, and then there was a howl.

55
00:04:19.411 --> 00:04:23.012
The wolves could hear Shere Khan tumbling about in the bushes.

56
00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.256
He was howling in pain.

57
00:04:25.276 --> 00:04:30.798
"That foolish tiger probably jumped at a human's campfire.

58
00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:34.679
It sounds like he burned his feet," Father Wolf said.

59
00:04:35.779 --> 00:04:38.900
Mother Wolf twitched one ear, listening carefully.

60
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.241
"Something is coming uphill!"

61
00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.682
The nearby bushes rustled.

62
00:04:45.762 --> 00:04:48.443
Father Wolf dropped low, ready to pounce.

63
00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.042
But then Mother Wolf let out a gasp.

64
00:04:54.062 --> 00:04:55.743
"It's a man cub!"

65
00:04:57.665 --> 00:05:00.787
A very young boy stood in front of the wolves.

66
00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:07.152
The tiny human blinked as he stared into Father Wolf's face.

67
00:05:07.172 --> 00:05:10.895
"Father!" Mother Wolf whispered.

68
00:05:10.915 --> 00:05:14.538
"Quick! Bring that man cub into our cave!"

69
00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:21.344
Father Wolf stepped forward and closed his jaws very gently on the child's neck.

70
00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:30.211
Then he carried the boy into the cave, dropping him near his own small cubs.
